  "text_pages": [
    "1. Courses Descriptions | Tohoku University\n1. Courses Descriptions\nLast Updated: Sep. 25, 2026\nTOP\n>\nFor International Students\n>\nExchange Programs\n>\nIPLA\n>\n1. Courses Descriptions\nCourse Descriptions\nIPLA 2026-2027\nFall\n*updated!\nJLPK - Japanese Language Program at Kawauchi\nIPLA 2026-2027\nFall\n*updated!\nCredits\n*updated!\n部局開講専門科目*履修について(日本語レベル５＆６の学生対象/Eligible for only Level 5 and 6 students)\n*科目やコース内容は変更される場合あり\n日本語レベル５\n**\n、６の学生は部局開講専門科目を履修することができます。\n科目についてはStudent Affairs Information System, QuickSyllabus, Syllabus Search Engineより検索可能です。\n-\nStudent Affairs Information System\n*DC Mail account required\n-\nQuickSyllabus\n*\nHow to Use\n-\nSyllabus Search Engine\nTips:\n-\nFuzzy String Searching\nis not available in our syllabus search engine, so search results are depending on your input (e.g. robotics, Robotics, ROBOTICS).\n**\nレベル５の学生は、履修したい科目の担当教員からの承認メールと別途フォーム(Registration Form for Specialized/General Education Subjects)を提出する必要があります/Those who are Level at 5 are required to submit an approval email from the class instructor and a separated form to the Student Exchange Division when you submit the online course registration form.\nPast Semesters\nPlease click the names of the classes on the timetable to see each syllabus.\nIPLA 2025-2026\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2024-2025\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2023-2024\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2022-2023\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2021-2022\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2020-2021\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2019-2020\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2018-2019\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2017-2018\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2016-2017\nFall\nSpring\nIPLA 2015-2016\nFall\nSpring\nPast Semesters (JLPK - Japanese Language Program at Kawauchi)\nIPLA 2025-2026　　Fall:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nSpring:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nIPLA 2024-2025　　Fall:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nSpring:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nIPLA 2023-2024　　Fall:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nSpring:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\nIPLA 2022-2023　　Fall:\nCredits\nSpring:\nJLPK Courses for IPLA\n/\nCredits\n2018 Fall - 2022 Fall\n過去の学期 (日本語レベル５＆６の学生対象)\n日本語レベル５＆６以上の学生向け日本語科目リスト\nIPLA Research Project\nThe IPLA Research Project is an independent study course focusing on a certain topic within your major or interest. The classes are conducted either one-on-one or in small groups. You will meet your instructor on a regular basis to confirm the progress of your research and complete the final paper by the end of the semester. It is an opportunity for you to deepen your studies at a higher level with professors at Tohoku University. Different topics will be offered each semester.\nPast Research Topics\n・Frontal Lobe Activity and its Relevance for the Theories of Action\n・Philosophy of Language\n・Child Labor in Cambodia"
